From 3e81f56a8e5f18e57a25ae4d6b1f6e7729240567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yanis <yanis@ameseder.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:24:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mfkey): Stack-Ueberlauf beim Nested-/Mfkey32-Recovery
 behoben
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

App-Stack 1 KB -> 2 KB, Worker-Thread 'MFKeyWorker' 2 KB -> 4 KB.
mfkey war mit 1 KB App-Stack die kleinste aller NFC-Apps (nfc_magic 4 KB,
picopass/seader 5 KB); der 2-KB-Worker sprengte bei tiefen Crypto1-
Aufrufketten + mehreren malloc-Bloecken den Stack -> harter Absturz.
FAP baut grün (APPCHK bestanden); On-Device-Test mit echten Nonces ausstehend.
---
 mfkey/application.fam | 2 +-
 mfkey/mfkey.c         | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mfkey/application.fam b/mfkey/application.fam
index 7fba499..7e9af6f 100644
--- a/mfkey/application.fam
+++ b/mfkey/application.fam
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ App(
         "gui",
         "storage",
     ],
-    stack_size=1 * 1024,
+    stack_size=2 * 1024,
     fap_icon="mfkey.png",
     fap_category="NFC",
     fap_author="@noproto",
diff --git a/mfkey/mfkey.c b/mfkey/mfkey.c
index 4448c88..282f39c 100644
--- a/mfkey/mfkey.c
+++ b/mfkey/mfkey.c
@@ -1324,7 +1324,7 @@ int32_t mfkey_main()
 	gui_add_view_port(gui, view_port, GuiLayerFullscreen);
 
 	program_state->mfkeythread =
-		furi_thread_alloc_ex("MFKeyWorker", 2048, mfkey_worker_thread, program_state);
+		furi_thread_alloc_ex("MFKeyWorker", 4096, mfkey_worker_thread, program_state);
 
 	InputEvent input_event;
 	for (bool main_loop = true; main_loop;)
-- 
2.54.0.windows.1

